                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">"Fundamentals of Medicine" is a compulsory professional course for students majoring in medicine and pharmacy. The content covers anatomy, histology, and physiology. Starting from the normal morphology of organ systems and histological structures, it studies the basic structures and functions of various tissues and organs in the human body, and clarifies the physiological activities and regulatory mechanisms of each system. This course focuses on the basic functions of cells, the nervous system, the circulatory system, the respiratory system, the urinary system, the endocrine system, the digestive system, etc., as well as the working principles of these organ systems and the pathophysiological mechanisms of related diseases. The physiological content involved in this course is a functional discipline that students come into contact with for the first time. Some of its teaching content is relatively abstract and difficult to understand. To strengthen the teaching effect, guided by learning outcomes and professional foundations, it emphasizes the profound impact of the course on students' subsequent learning and life from aspects such as core knowledge, applying what they have learned, drawing inferences from one another, and learning to learn. It actively considers the long-term effects of students' learning of the course, promotes students' continuous learning and value-added learning, and lays a solid foundation for their subsequent study of professional courses.</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:19.9000pt;">
                <td width=777 valign=center colspan=14 style="width:466.7000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-left-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
